00:32:47,230 --> 00:32:49,895
wouldn't it be better
if you slept with someone

510
00:32:49,896 --> 00:32:51,354
and then see if he stays or not?

511
00:32:51,355 --> 00:32:53,105
But I love him.

512
00:32:53,605 --> 00:32:55,270
It's his feelings I'm unsure about.

513
00:32:55,271 --> 00:32:57,479
I want to give him the chance
to walk out of it,

514
00:32:57,480 --> 00:32:58,771
if that's what he wants.

515
00:32:59,813 --> 00:33:02,730
Is it his love you want to test
or his character?

516
00:33:03,688 --> 00:33:05,896
If he shows interest in me
on his own, I'll understand.

517
00:33:06,355 --> 00:33:10,520
But if I'm throwing myself at him
and he still doesn't respond,

518
00:33:10,521 --> 00:33:12,146
then either he's dead from the waist down

519
00:33:12,730 --> 00:33:15,480
or has superhuman self-control.

520
00:33:16,313 --> 00:33:18,271
Okay, let's say he doesn't respond.

521
00:33:19,396 --> 00:33:22,855
Who's to say he won't end up
falling for another girl someday?

522
00:33:24,105 --> 00:33:25,188
It doesn't work this way.

523
00:33:25,688 --> 00:33:28,312
Feelings don't stick forever.

524
00:33:28,313 --> 00:33:29,730
Nothing's permanent.

525
00:33:30,313 --> 00:33:31,521
They can always change.

526
00:33:33,896 --> 00:33:35,313
Why are you overthinking this?

527
00:33:36,896 --> 00:33:37,896
It's a fun challenge.

528
00:33:39,271 --> 00:33:40,480
What do you have to lose?

529
00:33:41,063 --> 00:33:42,105
Are you sure?

530
00:33:43,146 --> 00:33:44,770
Because this "fun challenge"

531
00:33:44,771 --> 00:33:47,062
could destroy your perfectly
good relationship.

532
00:33:47,063 --> 00:33:48,312
I must tell you that.

533
00:33:48,313 --> 00:33:49,188
I'm sure.

534
00:33:50,813 --> 00:33:52,563
This could complicate our friendship too.

535
00:33:55,146 --> 00:33:56,563
It's been ten years since we last met.

536
00:33:56,980 --> 00:33:58,479
We're not such good friends.

537
00:33:58,480 --> 00:33:59,480
Ouch!

538
00:34:01,938 --> 00:34:02,938
Okay!

539
00:34:06,980 --> 00:34:10,063
By the way, I don't handle rejection well.

540
00:34:11,355 --> 00:34:14,771
So, if he doesn't respond to my flirting,
which never happens, by the way,

541
00:34:15,896 --> 00:34:18,605
and my ego gets bruised,
don't blame me.

542
00:34:19,521 --> 00:34:20,438
I won't.

543
00:34:25,438 --> 00:34:29,855
Okay, how far does he need to slip
before you believe he doesn't love you?

544
00:34:30,355 --> 00:34:31,230
What do you mean?

545
00:34:31,646 --> 00:34:34,646
I mean… this far?

546
00:34:36,105 --> 00:34:37,105
This far?

547
00:34:38,146 --> 00:34:40,270
- Or all the way…
- Okay, okay, okay, enough!

548
00:34:40,271 --> 00:34:41,896
That's enough to give me clarity.

549
00:34:45,521 --> 00:34:46,438
Kunal!

550
00:34:47,105 --> 00:34:49,312
- Wine.
- Yeah, that's the right one.

551
00:34:49,313 --> 00:34:50,355
What are you two talking about?

552
00:34:50,813 --> 00:34:51,855
Negotiating your price.

553
00:34:52,813 --> 00:34:54,896
I said, now that we've found
a diamond, we might as well bid for it.

554
00:34:55,771 --> 00:34:57,021
We were fixing the price.

555
00:34:57,605 --> 00:34:59,396
I'm not a diamond. I'm Kohinoor.

556
00:35:00,188 --> 00:35:02,230
It's not that easy to own me.

557
00:35:03,980 --> 00:35:05,021
Good night, ladies.

558
00:35:06,730 --> 00:35:08,063
Sorry.
Good night.

559
00:35:08,355 --> 00:35:10,021
You are gonna have a really good night.

560
00:35:11,105 --> 00:35:12,229
Good night, baby.

561
00:35:12,230 --> 00:35:14,563
- Nice ass.
- Wait. Hold on a second.

562
00:35:27,605 --> 00:35:29,021
Ciao, my bellas!

563
00:35:30,646 --> 00:35:31,605
Hi.

564
00:35:32,480 --> 00:35:33,479
Slept well?

565
00:35:33,480 --> 00:35:36,188
- Yeah.
- I'm here to cuddle with my baby.

566
00:35:36,771 --> 00:35:39,854
I spent two years in the hostel,
waking up to her alarm in her arms.

567
00:35:39,855 --> 00:35:41,562
- I too want to cuddle with my baby.
- Oh my God!

568
00:35:41,563 --> 00:35:44,438
Guys, guys, time out! God!

569
00:35:46,771 --> 00:35:49,188
Baby… you're not ticklish?

570
00:35:49,730 --> 00:35:50,646
What?

571
00:35:54,105 --> 00:35:56,146
She's not, but I am.

572
00:36:01,980 --> 00:36:03,605
Don't worry, it's okay.

573
00:36:05,063 --> 00:36:07,021
What's the hurry, darling?

574
00:36:07,396 --> 00:36:08,855
She won't get jealous of me.

575
00:36:09,688 --> 00:36:11,687
- Right?
- I'll manage.

576
00:36:11,688 --> 00:36:12,812
She may not get jealous,

577
00:36:12,813 --> 00:36:15,480
but you can't handle all this hotness.

578
00:36:16,021 --> 00:36:16,938
Try me.

579
00:36:18,063 --> 00:36:18,980
Breakfast?

580
00:36:19,438 --> 00:36:21,104
Listen, I'll join you in some time.

581
00:36:21,105 --> 00:36:22,771
I have two emails to send before that.

582
00:36:22,980 --> 00:36:23,896
Okay.

583
00:36:24,146 --> 00:36:25,021
I'll join you.

584
00:36:26,146 --> 00:36:27,605
Okay. So…

585
00:36:30,938 --> 00:36:33,563
{\an8}DANCE CLASS
LEARN TO DANCE

586
00:36:35,771 --> 00:36:37,063
Okay, this will be fun.

587
00:36:58,480 --> 00:36:59,521
Breakfast!

588
00:37:02,355 --> 00:37:05,313
If you're vacationing with me,
you need to loosen up a lot, my friend.

589
00:37:05,980 --> 00:37:08,771
Two drinks in,
and I'm completely loosened up.

590
00:37:10,021 --> 00:37:11,021
Can't wait.

591
00:37:22,896 --> 00:37:25,271
I need a guy's perspective
on something.

592
00:37:25,730 --> 00:37:27,063
Ask away. I'm a guy.

593
00:37:27,938 --> 00:37:29,355
Unsolicited opinions are my thing.

594
00:37:30,980 --> 00:37:34,146
Is there such a thing as
too much passion?

595
00:37:39,896 --> 00:37:40,854
What?

596
00:37:40,855 --> 00:37:43,771
Well, my last relationship,
or whatever it was,

597
00:37:44,605 --> 00:37:47,313
ended because he thought
that's all I ever wanted.

598
00:37:50,063 --> 00:37:51,480
He should've been happy, right?

599
00:37:53,021 --> 00:37:53,980
What do you think?

600
00:37:56,105 --> 00:37:57,188
You're a <i>narbhakshi.</i>

601
00:37:57,730 --> 00:37:58,687
What's that?

602
00:37:58,688 --> 00:38:01,646
<i>"Nar"</i> means man. Me.

603
00:38:02,271 --> 00:38:06,354
<i>"Bhakshi"</i> means eater. That's you.

604
00:38:06,355 --> 00:38:08,480
No, no, I'm serious.
From a guy's perspective,

605
00:38:09,063 --> 00:38:11,437
is being passionate really a bad thing?

606
00:38:11,438 --> 00:38:14,021
And who passes on an opportunity

607
00:38:14,521 --> 00:38:17,146
to have a purely physical relationship?

608
00:38:20,938 --> 00:38:21,896
With me.

609
00:38:30,771 --> 00:38:31,688
Would you?

610
00:38:42,188 --> 00:38:43,188
- Boo!
- Oh!

611
00:38:43,730 --> 00:38:45,313
Baby! Where were you?

612
00:38:45,813 --> 00:38:46,896
I was waiting for you.

613
00:38:47,230 --> 00:38:49,812
- I was finalizing today's plan.
- Yeah?

614
00:38:49,813 --> 00:38:51,896
I've booked us a vineyard tour.

615
00:38:52,313 --> 00:38:54,605
I have no interest
in watching wine being made.

616
00:38:55,438 --> 00:38:57,730
I've planned an architecture tour.

617
00:39:00,646 --> 00:39:02,021
It's her holiday.
She gets to decide.

618
00:39:02,688 --> 00:39:04,521
No, baby, it's okay.

619
00:39:04,855 --> 00:39:06,355
I know you'll get bored.

620
00:39:07,730 --> 00:39:09,063
You go with her.

621
00:39:09,646 --> 00:39:12,105
I'll see you both at dinner.

622
00:39:13,438 --> 00:39:16,437
No, we're on this holiday together.
We'll do everything together.

623
00:39:16,438 --> 00:39:18,062
Don't be silly.
I'll come with you, baby.

624
00:39:18,063 --> 00:39:20,895
Baby, we can do things
separately for one day.

625
00:39:20,896 --> 00:39:22,188
What's the big deal?

626
00:39:22,438 --> 00:39:23,313
Really?

627
00:39:25,021 --> 00:39:26,230
- Yeah.
- Come here.

628
00:39:33,313 --> 00:39:34,313
Shall we?

629
00:39:41,271 --> 00:39:42,437
- Miss…
- How much?

630
00:39:42,438 --> 00:39:43,895
A coppola for your handsome boyfriend?

631
00:39:43,896 --> 00:39:44,937
- No, no, no.
- Yeah…

632
00:39:44,938 --> 00:39:46,938
- I'm… I'm not her…
- Yes.

633
00:39:48,438 --> 00:39:49,855
I'll take…

634
00:39:52,521 --> 00:39:53,520
I'll pay for it.

635
00:39:53,521 --> 00:39:54,980
- You'll give a discount?
- It's okay, it's okay.

636
00:39:55,938 --> 00:39:57,480
I've conned plenty of guys before.

637
00:39:58,271 --> 00:40:00,355
You can join that distinguished list too.

638
00:40:07,146 --> 00:40:09,813
You reacted to the idea
of being my boyfriend

639
00:40:10,730 --> 00:40:12,396
as if I'd insulted you.

640
00:40:14,355 --> 00:40:15,313
Am I really that bad?

641
00:40:16,355 --> 00:40:18,063
No! Not at all.

642
00:40:18,438 --> 00:40:21,605
I just didn't want you to feel awkward.

643
00:40:23,605 --> 00:40:25,271
Who knows if I'm even your type?

644
00:40:26,855 --> 00:40:27,938
You are.

645
00:40:38,105 --> 00:40:39,271
Isn't it crazy?

646
00:40:41,146 --> 00:40:44,021
If you crush these ordinary grapes
the right way…

647
00:40:44,813 --> 00:40:48,646
at the right temperature, under the right
conditions, in the right barrel,

648
00:40:49,646 --> 00:40:51,188
leave them alone long enough,

649
00:40:52,105 --> 00:40:53,271
and they become
something extraordinary.

650
00:40:54,521 --> 00:40:55,855
You know, it's not just grapes.

651
00:40:56,313 --> 00:41:00,021
Apples, pears, cherries…

652
00:41:02,563 --> 00:41:03,980
every fruit carries a little intoxication.

653
00:41:06,688 --> 00:41:08,355
So you are passionate about something.

654
00:41:10,313 --> 00:41:11,271
Of course.

655
00:41:11,730 --> 00:41:13,271
What made you think I'm not passionate?

656
00:41:16,480 --> 00:41:17,980
What else are you passionate about?

657
00:41:18,355 --> 00:41:19,396
Food!

658
00:41:20,271 --> 00:41:21,895
Eating it and cooking it.

659
00:41:21,896 --> 00:41:23,271
It's no different, really.

660
00:41:23,646 --> 00:41:26,395
The right ingredients, a little patience,
a little time.

661
00:41:26,396 --> 00:41:27,271
Magic.

662
00:41:29,688 --> 00:41:30,563
Come with me.

663
00:41:31,063 --> 00:41:32,105
So, what's next?

664
00:41:40,896 --> 00:41:42,020
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

665
00:41:42,021 --> 00:41:43,020
Hello.

666
00:41:43,021 --> 00:41:46,813
Starting off with a light-bodied red
for the lovely couple.

667
00:41:48,188 --> 00:41:49,896
Go ahead, say it.

668
00:41:50,271 --> 00:41:52,688
Tell him we're not a couple.
We're just friends.

669
00:41:53,188 --> 00:41:55,146
If Diya heard, she'd lose it.

670
00:41:55,480 --> 00:41:56,896
It's not like that.

671
00:41:57,980 --> 00:41:59,605
I didn't mean it like that
back then either.

672
00:41:59,980 --> 00:42:01,438
There you go with the decency.

673
00:42:01,896 --> 00:42:03,605
What's wrong with men these days?

674
00:42:08,480 --> 00:42:10,520
Earlier, if I went out for drinks
with a guy,

675
00:42:10,521 --> 00:42:14,020
the first thing on his mind was
getting me drunk

676
00:42:14,021 --> 00:42:15,355
and taking advantage of me.

677
00:42:17,105 --> 00:42:20,896
Little did they know, ten guys
like them would've gone down

678
00:42:21,105 --> 00:42:22,938
before I even got out of my seat.

679
00:42:24,396 --> 00:42:25,813
Let the others take advantage.

680
00:42:26,688 --> 00:42:28,562
I'm happy to bear your loss with you.

681
00:42:28,563 --> 00:42:31,605
Oh… I like this Kunal.

682
00:42:42,646 --> 00:42:45,896
<i>Even if you want to run away
You never find an escape route</i>

683
00:42:48,146 --> 00:42:51,938
<i>Anyone who embraces you
Even for a moment</i>

684
00:42:54,188 --> 00:42:57,896
<i>Lives an entire lifetime in that moment</i>

685
00:42:58,938 --> 00:43:02,146
<i>If something burns
The smoke always shows</i>

686
00:43:02,563 --> 00:43:06,270
<i>I'm so lost in you
I don't even know how anymore</i>

687
00:43:06,271 --> 00:43:07,188
Careful…

688
00:43:09,188 --> 00:43:10,938
or you'll fall in love with me.

689
00:43:15,563 --> 00:43:17,313
It was a joke, man!

690
00:43:18,813 --> 00:43:20,396
There goes my fantasy!

691
00:43:20,813 --> 00:43:22,730
Car breaks down on a highway.

692
00:43:23,021 --> 00:43:24,438
I'm stranded.

693
00:43:25,063 --> 00:43:28,730
And a dreamy man plays the guitar
to entertain me.

694
00:43:30,396 --> 00:43:35,230
Oh, I forgot to ask Diya
where we're meeting for dinner.

695
00:43:35,480 --> 00:43:36,646
- One second.
- What's the hurry?

696
00:43:40,063 --> 00:43:41,730
Live in the moment, my friend.

697
00:43:45,021 --> 00:43:46,771
Come here. Sit.
Sit down.

698
00:43:47,730 --> 00:43:51,646
I don't know about those ten guys
you've been with before…

699
00:43:52,646 --> 00:43:54,521
but you've definitely folded.

700
00:43:55,063 --> 00:43:56,062
No.

701
00:43:56,063 --> 00:43:57,188
Here, drink this water.

702
00:43:58,646 --> 00:44:02,646
My legs aren't strong enough
to carry you back.

703
00:44:03,480 --> 00:44:05,021
- At least try.
- Go on, drink it.

704
00:44:11,105 --> 00:44:12,063
Thank you.

705
00:44:26,396 --> 00:44:27,313
Anshul!

706
00:44:27,896 --> 00:44:28,896
Goosebumps.

707
00:44:30,646 --> 00:44:32,145
Don't make any plans tomorrow.

708
00:44:32,146 --> 00:44:33,771
- We're going on a road trip.
- Okay.

709
00:44:35,271 --> 00:44:36,480
I'll just freshen up and come.

710
00:44:37,563 --> 00:44:38,980
Wait. I'll come too.

711
00:44:39,563 --> 00:44:40,521
One second.

712
00:44:42,230 --> 00:44:43,146
Nothing!

713
00:44:43,355 --> 00:44:45,770
I went at him like a sizzling hot dish,

714
00:44:45,771 --> 00:44:48,938
and he kept rejecting me like
yesterday's stale leftovers.

715
00:44:50,105 --> 00:44:51,271
What's wrong with him?

716
00:44:51,438 --> 00:44:53,270
Seriously, what is wrong with him?

717
00:44:53,271 --> 00:44:54,729
Give it time.

718
00:44:54,730 --> 00:44:55,980
Maybe try harder.

719
00:44:56,646 --> 00:44:58,395
You know, I think he's not responding

720
00:44:58,396 --> 00:45:01,271
because he doesn't want
to seem like a player or a cheater.

721
00:45:03,146 --> 00:45:04,979
You'll have to nudge a little too.

722
00:45:04,980 --> 00:45:06,313
But what do I do?

723
00:45:06,855 --> 00:45:08,812
Maybe just try and push him away.

724
00:45:08,813 --> 00:45:11,895
Get him out of this
lovey-dovey holiday zone.

725
00:45:11,896 --> 00:45:12,979
- Do something!
- Okay, okay!

726
00:45:12,980 --> 00:45:13,896
Come on, Diya!

727
00:45:15,771 --> 00:45:18,062
Why do girls always go
to the bathroom together?

728
00:45:18,063 --> 00:45:20,688
Do your pee cycles sync too?

729
00:45:22,980 --> 00:45:24,938
Could you think before you speak for once?

730
00:45:28,771 --> 00:45:32,187
Baby, I just said pee cycle--

731
00:45:32,188 --> 00:45:33,563
Everything's a joke to you!

732
00:45:33,980 --> 00:45:36,855
At least look around
before blurting things out!

733
00:45:37,271 --> 00:45:38,730
It's okay, relax.

734
00:45:38,980 --> 00:45:40,146
It's just me.

735
00:45:40,813 --> 00:45:42,146
What's the big deal?

736
00:45:44,146 --> 00:45:46,355
Should we order?
I'm so hungry.

737
00:45:46,771 --> 00:45:47,980
Baby, you order.

738
00:45:48,688 --> 00:45:49,771
You know this stuff better.

739
00:45:52,063 --> 00:45:53,063
Pass me the menu.

740
00:45:53,771 --> 00:45:55,188
You handle his order. I'll handle mine.

741
00:45:57,605 --> 00:45:58,521
Please.

742
00:45:59,813 --> 00:46:00,730
Sure.

743
00:46:04,105 --> 00:46:05,980
You know what I would
love to have right now?

744
00:46:06,480 --> 00:46:07,438
<i>Kadhi chawal.</i>

745
00:46:09,855 --> 00:46:12,104
That's the only thing I miss from India.

746
00:46:12,105 --> 00:46:13,855
You should've told me!

747
00:46:14,688 --> 00:46:16,271
I would've made <i>kadhi chawal</i> for her.

748
00:46:17,271 --> 00:46:18,855
When was the last time you cooked?

749
00:46:21,230 --> 00:46:22,855
"I would've made it," he says!

750
00:46:32,980 --> 00:46:34,396
Sorry, guys. Sorry.

751
00:46:49,855 --> 00:46:51,688
Kunal, shut the window!

752
00:46:53,646 --> 00:46:54,980
Baby, why are you sleeping here?

753
00:46:55,396 --> 00:46:57,230
- I'm really sorry about last night--
- Shut up!

754
00:46:57,355 --> 00:46:58,771
My head is exploding.

755
00:46:59,646 --> 00:47:01,105
Ciao, my bellas!

756
00:47:03,146 --> 00:47:04,938
Ready for the trip of your lives, guys?

757
00:47:07,063 --> 00:47:08,270
What?

758
00:47:08,271 --> 00:47:09,770
Her head's exploding.

759
00:47:09,771 --> 00:47:11,271
She gets bad migraines.

760
00:47:12,646 --> 00:47:15,145
I think we might have to cancel the trip.

761
00:47:15,146 --> 00:47:16,729
- No!
- Yeah!

762
00:47:16,730 --> 00:47:19,146
- Kunal!
- Sorry. Sorry, baby.

763
00:47:21,230 --> 00:47:23,105
I booked such a sexy villa.

764
00:47:23,688 --> 00:47:25,813
And it's all non-refundable, you know?

765
00:47:26,938 --> 00:47:28,354
But it's okay.

766
00:47:28,355 --> 00:47:29,605
It's just money. It's fine.

767
00:47:30,730 --> 00:47:32,480
No, no, it's not okay.

768
00:47:32,605 --> 00:47:35,188
You two go ahead.
I'll join you tomorrow.

769
00:47:35,688 --> 00:47:36,687
Meaning?

770
00:47:36,688 --> 00:47:38,729
There's no point in you staying back.

771
00:47:38,730 --> 00:47:40,229
