We've known each other forever.

1521
01:38:52,355 --> 01:38:53,479
Yeah.

1522
01:38:53,480 --> 01:38:54,896
Come on, guys.
It was my idea.

1523
01:38:56,063 --> 01:38:57,021
Want something to drink?

1524
01:38:58,146 --> 01:38:59,104
Anybody else?

1525
01:38:59,105 --> 01:39:00,062
- Me.
- I'm good.

1526
01:39:00,063 --> 01:39:01,563
Smile, guys! Come on!

1527
01:39:01,855 --> 01:39:03,145
Yay, bachelor party!

1528
01:39:03,146 --> 01:39:04,563
Let's have a devotional gathering, guys!

1529
01:39:05,146 --> 01:39:07,687
Look, you'll have to respect
the traditions.

1530
01:39:07,688 --> 01:39:08,979
And all of them.
Right, guys?

1531
01:39:08,980 --> 01:39:09,937
- Right.
- Correct.

1532
01:39:09,938 --> 01:39:10,979
And as your bridesmaid,

1533
01:39:10,980 --> 01:39:13,479
it's my duty to throw you a bachelorette.

1534
01:39:13,480 --> 01:39:16,604
- So plan the youngsters' party.
- What even is a youngsters' party?

1535
01:39:16,605 --> 01:39:18,229
- Who does that? Come on, guys!
- Baby.

1536
01:39:18,230 --> 01:39:19,521
- Youngsters…
- Yeah!

1537
01:39:20,605 --> 01:39:23,480
Here's what I think.
If we're doing all the rituals anyway,

1538
01:39:23,605 --> 01:39:25,480
might as well do this one too.

1539
01:39:26,480 --> 01:39:28,563
- What do you think?
- No, I…

1540
01:39:29,021 --> 01:39:31,145
- Please, Diya…
- Come on, Diya!

1541
01:39:31,146 --> 01:39:33,270
- Come on!
- Please!

1542
01:39:33,271 --> 01:39:34,520
- Come on!
- Please.

1543
01:39:34,521 --> 01:39:36,312
- Come on!
- Come on!

1544
01:39:36,313 --> 01:39:37,479
- Please…
- Fine!

1545
01:39:37,480 --> 01:39:39,437
- Fine! Fine!
- Okay!

1546
01:39:39,438 --> 01:39:40,605
I love you!

1547
01:39:44,230 --> 01:39:46,480
For letting me throw
the best party for her!

1548
01:39:48,480 --> 01:39:49,855
- Wow!
- Yeah!

1549
01:39:50,021 --> 01:39:50,938
You're welcome.

1550
01:39:51,521 --> 01:39:52,771
I didn't say "thank you," idiot.

1551
01:39:53,438 --> 01:39:54,313
I said, "Love you."

1552
01:39:56,230 --> 01:39:58,105
It won't kill you to say, "Love you too."

1553
01:40:02,146 --> 01:40:03,105
Okay. I love you too.

1554
01:40:03,730 --> 01:40:04,646
Happy?

1555
01:40:10,146 --> 01:40:12,229
Should we plan this, guys? Yeah?

1556
01:40:12,230 --> 01:40:13,645
This is a great idea. I love it.

1557
01:40:13,646 --> 01:40:15,313
- Thank you for the farmhouse, but…
- But, but…

1558
01:40:19,313 --> 01:40:21,187
Let's go, boys. Let's go.

1559
01:40:21,188 --> 01:40:22,271
Time to party!

1560
01:40:29,396 --> 01:40:30,313
What are you doing here?

1561
01:40:38,813 --> 01:40:39,896
Remember the vineyard?

1562
01:40:40,980 --> 01:40:41,855
Yeah.

1563
01:40:44,355 --> 01:40:45,313
Have fun.

1564
01:40:47,688 --> 01:40:48,646
Where are you going?

1565
01:40:50,896 --> 01:40:52,105
I just came to give you this.

1566
01:40:54,521 --> 01:40:56,688
I have another party to set up.

1567
01:40:57,146 --> 01:40:58,355
Won't you stay for a drink?

1568
01:41:00,313 --> 01:41:01,313
I'll stay…

1569
01:41:02,730 --> 01:41:03,855
but what will you tell Diya?

1570
01:41:04,313 --> 01:41:05,271
One drink.

1571
01:41:08,563 --> 01:41:09,480
Okay.

1572
01:41:14,980 --> 01:41:17,105
I've never seen you this quiet.

1573
01:41:22,313 --> 01:41:23,230
What's wrong?

1574
01:41:28,271 --> 01:41:29,146
Nothing.

1575
01:41:31,813 --> 01:41:32,688
It's nice.

1576
01:41:38,105 --> 01:41:41,605
Never thought my love could
stress someone out like this.

1577
01:41:43,313 --> 01:41:50,313
I always thought the man I loved would
be thrilled to know I loved him.

1578
01:41:54,688 --> 01:41:58,271
If it's bothering you so much,
just forget I said anything.

1579
01:41:59,938 --> 01:42:00,980
How can I forget?

1580
01:42:04,396 --> 01:42:06,396
These aren't things you forget, Ally.

1581
01:42:10,605 --> 01:42:14,145
You've said "I love you,"

1582
01:42:14,146 --> 01:42:17,230
but I don't think you even know
what love really is.

1583
01:42:20,355 --> 01:42:21,271
Okay.

1584
01:42:21,896 --> 01:42:25,021
Maybe I'm not familiar with
all this "textbook wisdom."

1585
01:42:28,605 --> 01:42:32,938
But I know what I feel for you…

1586
01:42:35,438 --> 01:42:36,396
is love.

1587
01:42:37,980 --> 01:42:39,438
You love me,

1588
01:42:41,396 --> 01:42:43,771
but it doesn't bother you that…

1589
01:42:45,730 --> 01:42:46,771
we're not together?

1590
01:42:47,688 --> 01:42:48,646
Of course it bothers me.

1591
01:42:50,146 --> 01:42:51,271
But what can I do?

1592
01:42:53,980 --> 01:42:56,855
And I love you…

1593
01:42:59,605 --> 01:43:02,771
but you never said you feel the same.

1594
01:43:14,438 --> 01:43:17,604
<i>Hear my prayers, before you I bow alone</i>

1595
01:43:17,605 --> 01:43:20,520
Okay then… I guess that's my cue.

1596
01:43:20,521 --> 01:43:23,562
<i>Bulleya, I've forgotten the way back home</i>

1597
01:43:23,563 --> 01:43:27,021
Ally, Ally, Ally!
Where are you going?

1598
01:43:28,063 --> 01:43:30,938
Stay with us.
We'll have the night of a lifetime.

1599
01:43:31,730 --> 01:43:33,062
Thanks for the offer, man,

1600
01:43:33,063 --> 01:43:35,355
but I've got bridesmaid duty.
Sorry.

1601
01:43:35,896 --> 01:43:37,604
Ally, you sure I can't convince you?

1602
01:43:37,605 --> 01:43:39,188
- Diya's gonna kill me, bro.
- Hey!

1603
01:43:40,355 --> 01:43:41,813
Think before you speak.

1604
01:43:43,480 --> 01:43:45,688
You're not a kid.
Is that any way to talk to a girl?

1605
01:43:46,063 --> 01:43:47,437
"Night of a lifetime!"

1606
01:43:47,438 --> 01:43:49,520
I meant at the party.

1607
01:43:49,521 --> 01:43:52,145
Then rehearse it in your head
before you say it!

1608
01:43:52,146 --> 01:43:53,770
Kunal… it's okay.

1609
01:43:53,771 --> 01:43:55,604
I'm sure he didn't mean that.

1610
01:43:55,605 --> 01:43:56,855
- Idiot!
- It's fine.

1611
01:43:57,188 --> 01:43:58,730
We're good, okay?

1612
01:43:59,980 --> 01:44:01,354
- Bye.
- Bye.

1613
01:44:01,355 --> 01:44:06,230
<i>Bulleya, I've forgotten the way back home</i>

1614
01:44:06,355 --> 01:44:11,729
<i>Hear my prayers, before you I bow alone</i>

1615
01:44:11,730 --> 01:44:12,730
<i>Bulleya…</i>

1616
01:44:14,105 --> 01:44:15,937
- Guys!
- There's a lot!

1617
01:44:15,938 --> 01:44:17,063
That's it?

1618
01:44:18,646 --> 01:44:20,063
Come on, guys, get up!

1619
01:44:20,188 --> 01:44:21,563
Give me, give me, give me.

1620
01:44:27,313 --> 01:44:28,854
- Oh God…
- What are you doing?

1621
01:44:28,855 --> 01:44:29,812
Give me my phone.

1622
01:44:29,813 --> 01:44:31,395
- Absolutely not.
- Ally…

1623
01:44:31,396 --> 01:44:33,896
You can talk to Kunal
for the rest of your life.

1624
01:44:34,438 --> 01:44:37,187
Tonight, you're single.

1625
01:44:37,188 --> 01:44:38,605
And you're with me.

1626
01:44:39,021 --> 01:44:40,063
Ally…

1627
01:44:40,396 --> 01:44:43,063
Smile, my love.
We're not mourning.

1628
01:44:43,896 --> 01:44:45,855
We're kicking off
your wedding celebrations.

1629
01:44:46,396 --> 01:44:47,271
See?

1630
01:44:55,855 --> 01:44:58,105
<i>The number you are calling
is not answering.</i>

1631
01:45:12,480 --> 01:45:17,980
<i>Bulleya, I've forgotten the way back home</i>

1632
01:45:18,105 --> 01:45:23,895
<i>Hear my prayers, before you I bow alone</i>

1633
01:45:23,896 --> 01:45:29,395
<i>Bulleya, I've forgotten the way back home</i>

1634
01:45:29,396 --> 01:45:32,479
<i>Hear my prayers</i>

1635
01:45:32,480 --> 01:45:35,062
- Nice.
<i>- Before you I bow alone</i>

1636
01:45:35,063 --> 01:45:40,770
<i>It kept wandering, this lost drifter</i>

1637
01:45:40,771 --> 01:45:43,229
- Lift.
<i>- My poor heart is</i>

1638
01:45:43,230 --> 01:45:46,270
- Careful!
<i>- Caught on you forever.</i>

1639
01:45:46,271 --> 01:45:52,021
<i>Lift this veil of silence at last</i>

1640
01:45:52,146 --> 01:45:57,645
<i>Such a moment may never come back</i>

1641
01:45:57,646 --> 01:46:01,854
<i>Fulfill the longing of my heart</i>

1642
01:46:01,855 --> 01:46:02,771
Stop the car.

1643
01:46:04,771 --> 01:46:05,646
Stop the car.

1644
01:46:06,188 --> 01:46:09,104
- What happened?
<i>- Before I fall apart…</i>

1645
01:46:09,105 --> 01:46:12,230
<i>Bulleya, I've forgotten the way…</i>

1646
01:46:23,688 --> 01:46:24,730
What did you think?

1647
01:46:28,355 --> 01:46:29,563
You'd say "I love you…"

1648
01:46:31,521 --> 01:46:32,896
and I'd leave Diya?

1649
01:46:36,480 --> 01:46:37,605
Leave a girl…

1650
01:46:38,938 --> 01:46:42,646
four days before her wedding?

1651
01:46:45,021 --> 01:46:46,688
Embarrass her in front of everyone?

1652
01:46:50,938 --> 01:46:52,688
Just because you think…

1653
01:46:55,146 --> 01:46:57,230
you and I are better together?

1654
01:47:02,021 --> 01:47:03,105
You don't think so?

1655
01:47:11,813 --> 01:47:12,688
No, I don't.

1656
01:47:19,480 --> 01:47:20,355
You sure?

1657
01:47:21,688 --> 01:47:22,605
I'm sure.

1658
01:47:31,980 --> 01:47:35,980
You can't leave Diya,
but you can at least be honest.

1659
01:47:51,980 --> 01:47:54,813
- I'll open it, Kunal, just…
- No, I'm good…

1660
01:47:58,521 --> 01:47:59,813
What are you two doing together?

1661
01:48:00,563 --> 01:48:01,938
I called you, baby.

1662
01:48:03,480 --> 01:48:05,605
You didn't answer,
so she came to get me.

1663
01:48:06,021 --> 01:48:07,021
Where's my phone?

1664
01:48:07,730 --> 01:48:09,729
Oh, shit! I'm so sorry.

1665
01:48:09,730 --> 01:48:11,604
I took it from you
and dropped it in my bag.

1666
01:48:11,605 --> 01:48:13,270
- I didn't realize.
- Yeah, right.

1667
01:48:13,271 --> 01:48:15,688
- Yeah, right.
- I saw your missed call.

1668
01:48:17,355 --> 01:48:19,355
I called you so many times,
but you never answered.

1669
01:48:20,480 --> 01:48:22,521
So, I asked her to come pick me up.

1670
01:48:22,646 --> 01:48:23,771
Why didn't you tell me?

1671
01:48:24,688 --> 01:48:26,771
You were asleep.
I didn't want to bother you.

1672
01:48:27,188 --> 01:48:28,854
He just needed a ride, so I picked him up.

1673
01:48:28,855 --> 01:48:30,104
You should've told me!

1674
01:48:30,105 --> 01:48:31,646
She just told you, didn't she?

1675
01:48:34,730 --> 01:48:36,271
She didn't want to bother you.

1676
01:48:37,521 --> 01:48:38,396
What is wrong with you?

1677
01:49:22,896 --> 01:49:23,771
Hey!

1678
01:49:23,938 --> 01:49:24,979
Hey!

1679
01:49:24,980 --> 01:49:25,938
Can you…

1680
01:49:27,730 --> 01:49:28,687
Sorry.

1681
01:49:28,688 --> 01:49:31,355
Could you move into a hotel for tonight?

1682
01:49:32,188 --> 01:49:33,105
Why?

1683
01:49:33,771 --> 01:49:35,938
It's our last night in this house
before the wedding.

1684
01:49:36,063 --> 01:49:38,105
We'll no longer be
boyfriend and girlfriend.

1685
01:49:38,271 --> 01:49:39,313
We'll be husband and wife.

1686
01:49:39,938 --> 01:49:43,605
I just want to spend this last day…

1687
01:49:46,688 --> 01:49:47,980
alone with him.

1688
01:49:52,563 --> 01:49:54,855
If you're insecure, just say it.

1689
01:49:55,938 --> 01:49:58,646
Why? Is there something
to be insecure about?

1690
01:49:59,563 --> 01:50:00,521
Maybe.

1691
01:50:03,438 --> 01:50:04,480
You were right.

1692
01:50:05,188 --> 01:50:07,771
You don't handle rejection gracefully.

1693
01:50:08,855 --> 01:50:12,896
But I didn't think you'd stoop this low.

1694
01:50:15,063 --> 01:50:16,521
What are you trying to prove?

1695
01:50:17,021 --> 01:50:18,980
I don't need to prove anything to anyone.

1696
01:50:21,855 --> 01:50:23,355
I just love Kunal.

1697
01:50:24,980 --> 01:50:26,021
I love him.

1698
01:50:26,605 --> 01:50:27,938
What? No…

1699
01:50:28,938 --> 01:50:31,230
And I've already told him how I feel.

1700
01:50:33,063 --> 01:50:34,188
He didn't tell you?

1701
01:50:37,605 --> 01:50:38,605
Oops.

1702
01:50:43,146 --> 01:50:44,188
What did he say?

1703
01:50:47,813 --> 01:50:49,688
Isn't it sad that you have to ask me?

1704
01:50:51,730 --> 01:50:53,021
But actually that's the point.

1705
01:50:53,563 --> 01:50:55,855
First love isn't always true love, Diya.

1706
01:50:57,605 --> 01:50:59,480
You met him first. That's your luck.

1707
01:51:00,188 --> 01:51:02,313
Doesn't mean you're right for him.

1708
01:51:03,063 --> 01:51:06,105
Maybe I found him too late,
but I love him.

1709
01:51:07,105 --> 01:51:09,896
So I'm supposed to sacrifice my love
just because you met him first?

1710
01:51:10,563 --> 01:51:11,771
How does that make sense?

1711
01:51:12,313 --> 01:51:13,521
Especially when he…

1712
01:51:23,438 --> 01:51:24,313
Don't worry.

1713
01:51:25,480 --> 01:51:26,521
I'm not a home-wrecker.

1714
01:51:27,730 --> 01:51:30,105
But I still have the right
to stop this wedding.

1715
01:51:32,313 --> 01:51:34,063
And till the vows are taken,
I'm not giving up.

1716
01:51:37,230 --> 01:51:38,396
If he takes them with you, he's yours.

1717
01:51:39,980 --> 01:51:41,146
If I can stop them, he's mine.

1718
01:51:43,771 --> 01:51:45,480
I've known Kunal since we were kids.

1719
01:51:47,188 --> 01:51:49,438
For as long as I can remember,
we've been together.

1720
01:51:50,980 --> 01:51:53,270
You've known him for a month.

1721
01:51:53,271 --> 01:51:55,063
That's not love.

1722
01:51:56,021 --> 01:51:57,230
That's confusion.

1723
01:51:59,605 --> 01:52:02,688
Fine, so you told Kunal you love him.

1724
01:52:03,230 --> 01:52:04,980
But did you also tell him

1725
01:52:05,313 --> 01:52:07,354
you've been trying to stop this wedding?

1726
01:52:07,355 --> 01:52:08,313
Oh, wait!

1727
01:52:08,980 --> 01:52:11,063
You wouldn't risk looking so bad

1728
01:52:11,896 --> 01:52:14,396
before the man you love.

1729
01:52:15,980 --> 01:52:17,312
You're right.

1730
01:52:17,313 --> 01:52:20,605
Can't look so bad
in the eyes of the guy

1731
01:52:20,938 --> 01:52:22,313
you are about to marry.

1732
01:52:23,646 --> 01:52:26,105
Does Kunal know you asked me
to seduce him?

1733
01:52:32,521 --> 01:52:33,521
No?

1734
01:52:34,730 --> 01:52:36,688
Our friendship has no value for you.

1735
01:52:38,688 --> 01:52:39,896
We're not such good friends.

1736
01:52:44,146 --> 01:52:46,396
You're up already?
How are you feeling?

1737
01:52:47,188 --> 01:52:48,563
A bad one, baby.

1738
01:52:49,146 --> 01:52:50,146
I need my…

1739
01:52:50,438 --> 01:52:52,896
Sit back.
I'll make your hangover cure.

1740
01:52:53,521 --> 01:52:54,730
Already made one.

1741
01:52:55,230 --> 01:52:56,230
My special recipe.

1742
01:52:56,980 --> 01:52:59,146
Mine's worked on him for years.

1743
01:52:59,563 --> 01:53:01,895
If he tries mine,
he'll ask for it for years.

1744
01:53:01,896 --> 01:53:02,771
Come, have it.

1745
01:53:03,813 --> 01:53:05,855
Have it.

1746
01:53:06,230 --> 01:53:07,146
Like it?

1747
01:53:07,813 --> 01:53:09,520
- Better than the usual one, right?
- Water…

1748
01:53:09,521 --> 01:53:11,063
Oh, my poor baby!

1749
01:53:12,230 --> 01:53:15,105
Just lie down for ten minutes.
You'll be fine.

1750
01:53:16,521 --> 01:53:19,020
So, this time the booze was dodgy,
or it just didn't hit?

1751
01:53:19,021 --> 01:53:21,520
No chance of the booze being dodgy.

1752
01:53:21,521 --> 01:53:24,230
I specially got him
his favorite wine from Sicily.

1753
01:53:26,688 --> 01:53:31,313
Remember when you ditched us
and we went on our vineyard "date"?

1754
01:53:32,230 --> 01:53:33,355
We just fell in love…

1755
01:53:34,771 --> 01:53:35,855
with the wine.

1756
01:53:36,063 --> 01:53:36,938
Too good, right?

1757
01:53:38,021 --> 01:53:40,480
No matter how good
or special the booze is,

1758
01:53:40,688 --> 01:53:41,938
or where it's from,

1759
01:53:42,063 --> 01:53:44,355
the high wears off by morning.

1760
01:53:44,521 --> 01:53:45,688
After that,

1761
01:53:45,938 --> 01:53:48,354
only my hangover cure works.
Have it.

1762
01:53:48,355 --> 01:53:50,104
- Don't be jealous, baby.
- It's okay.

1763
01:53:50,105 --> 01:53:51,896
Being your bridesmaid was your gift.

1764
01:53:52,313 --> 01:53:53,646
But I had to give him something too.

1765
01:53:53,938 --> 01:53:56,146
Someone has to attend
to this poor child.

1766
01:53:56,521 --> 01:53:58,563
He gets plenty of attention.

1767
01:53:59,105 --> 01:54:00,271
And I'm not jealous.

1768
01:54:00,688 --> 01:54:02,521
Oh, right! I forgot.

1769
01:54:02,938 --> 01:54:04,271
This "diya" has no flame.

1770
01:54:05,063 --> 01:54:08,230
No light. No warmth.

1771
01:54:09,021 --> 01:54:10,021
It's just there.

1772
01:54:10,855 --> 01:54:12,480
- No baby. It's okay.
- Come on, get ready quickly.

1773
01:54:12,688 --> 01:54:13,979
We need to go shopping.

1774
01:54:13,980 --> 01:54:14,896
Shopping for what?

1775
01:54:16,855 --> 01:54:17,938
For your gift.

1776
01:54:18,313 --> 01:54:19,188
It's a surprise.

1777
01:54:21,063 --> 01:54:23,062
It's a surprise.
Come, come.

1778
01:54:23,063 --> 01:54:25,062
- I don't need any surprises! Kunal!
- What would you do without me?

1779
01:54:25,063 --> 01:54:26,020
Come.

1780
01:54:26,021 --> 01:54:26,896
Go get ready.

1781
01:54:31,771 --> 01:54:33,521
You think only you can surprise people?

1782
01:54:34,396 --> 01:54:35,521
Like the engagement ring?

1783
01:54:37,105 --> 01:54:39,230
You should've seen his face.

1784
01:54:40,021 --> 01:54:41,438
He was so not ready for it.

1785
01:54:44,230 --> 01:54:45,730
I'll go get ready, okay?

1786
01:55:14,021 --> 01:55:15,730
How will you know just by holding it up?

1787
01:55:16,396 --> 01:55:17,271
Come.

1788
01:55:19,938 --> 01:55:20,938
Help me out.

1789
01:55:45,646 --> 01:55:46,688
You okay?

1790
01:56:01,146 --> 01:56:02,688
That's my boy.

1791
01:56:07,688 --> 01:56:08,563
Cheers.

1792
01:56:14,438 --> 01:56:15,313
Papa…

1793
01:56:17,313 --> 01:56:20,063
How long have you and Mom been together?

1794
01:56:22,605 --> 01:56:23,855
Around 34 or 35 years.

1795
01:56:29,855 --> 01:56:32,855
In all these years,
did you ever feel someone else

1796
01:56:35,355 --> 01:56:38,021
might've been better for either of you?

1797
01:56:40,230 --> 01:56:42,771
It was a perfect match!

1798
01:56:45,355 --> 01:56:49,521
In fact, your mother should thank God.

1799
01:56:49,980 --> 01:56:52,271
Where'd she find a better man than me?

1800
01:56:52,396 --> 01:56:54,021
Someone who's still putting up with her?!

1801
01:57:07,730 --> 01:57:11,479
Son, pre-wedding jitters, getting nervous,
and having doubts

1802
01:57:11,480 --> 01:57:12,980
are completely normal.

1803
01:57:14,146 --> 01:57:16,063
Have a couple of drinks and sleep it off.

1804
01:57:17,146 --> 01:57:18,645
Tomorrow morning,
we set off for Chandigarh,

1805
01:57:18,646 --> 01:57:20,605
and we'll play <i>antakshari</i> all the way
till we reach.

1806
01:57:21,521 --> 01:57:26,105
And then the rituals will take place…

1807
01:57:27,313 --> 01:57:29,646
and before you know it,
it'll all be over.

1808
01:57:31,230 --> 01:57:32,146
Cheers!

1809
01:57:55,646 --> 01:57:57,312
- Listen up, everybody!
- Yes?

1810
01:57:57,313 --> 01:57:59,104
We're playing <i>antakshari</i> now.

1811
01:57:59,105 --> 01:58:01,062
- No!
- Yes!

1812
01:58:01,063 --> 01:58:02,145
Please, please, please!

1813
01:58:02,146 --> 01:58:03,812
We're not going to play A for <i>antakshari.</i>

1814
01:58:03,813 --> 01:58:05,355
- Why?
- Because it's B for boring!

1815
01:58:07,188 --> 01:58:08,355
I know a game.

1816
01:58:09,063 --> 01:58:10,020
"Love check."

1817
01:58:10,021 --> 01:58:12,520
- Oh!
- Spicy.

1818
01:58:12,521 --> 01:58:13,479
Let's go.

1819
01:58:13,480 --> 01:58:16,563
Let's see how well the bride
and groom know each other.

1820
01:58:16,938 --> 01:58:18,896
Interesting. I like it.

1821
01:58:20,146 --> 01:58:21,687
- I'll ask the questions.
- Bring it on!

1822
01:58:21,688 --> 01:58:23,188
It's a rapid fire, so be quick.

1823
01:58:23,521 --> 01:58:24,771
- Ready?
- Bring it on.

1824
01:58:25,188 --> 01:58:26,271
Alright!

1825
01:58:27,271 --> 01:58:28,271
Diya's favorite color?

1826
01:58:28,855 --> 01:58:30,062
- Orange.
- Baby blue.

1827
01:58:30,063 --> 01:58:31,187
Baby blue?

1828
01:58:31,188 --> 01:58:32,855
- That was just the first answer!
- Minus one.

1829
01:58:32,980 --> 01:58:34,395
- Next one. Next one.
- Stupid question.

1830
01:58:34,396 --> 01:58:35,562
- They're still warming up.
- They can do it.

1831
01:58:35,563 --> 01:58:36,896
- First question.
- Once more.

1832
01:58:38,771 --> 01:58:39,937
Kunal's favorite food?

1833
01:58:39,938 --> 01:58:41,146
<i>- Chole bhature.
- Rajma… bhature.</i>

1834
01:58:41,438 --> 01:58:42,896
<i>Rajma bhature?!</i>

1835
01:58:43,271 --> 01:58:44,480
Innovation.

1836
01:58:44,605 --> 01:58:45,855
He's a <i>rajma</i> fan!

1837
01:58:47,063 --> 01:58:48,730
Let's get romantic.

1838
01:58:49,688 --> 01:58:50,770
Where was your first kiss?

1839
01:58:50,771 --> 01:58:51,938
- My…
- In the car, right?

1840
01:58:55,021 --> 01:58:56,730
Babe… bedroom.

1841
01:58:59,188 --> 01:59:01,855
Alright, let's make it simple.

1842
01:59:03,021 --> 01:59:04,480
Who said "I love you" first?

1843
01:59:04,605 --> 01:59:05,730
- She did.
- He…

1844
01:59:11,105 --> 01:59:13,688
Are you sure you've known
each other for 16 years?

1845
01:59:15,438 --> 01:59:18,646
Well, I guess that's the sign
of a successful relationship.

1846
01:59:19,396 --> 01:59:20,313
Confusion.

1847
01:59:25,230 --> 01:59:27,646
Okay, enough with this stupid game!

1848
01:59:28,021 --> 01:59:30,563
- Let's just play <i>antakshari.</i>
- Yes!

1849
01:59:30,730 --> 01:59:33,145
Two teams!
Team A and Team B.

1850
01:59:33,146 --> 01:59:34,230
- That's it.
- Okay, done.

1851
01:59:54,646 --> 01:59:56,146
I remembered all those things.

1852
01:59:58,021 --> 01:59:59,438
I don't know, in the moment…

1853
02:00:01,396 --> 02:00:02,271
I forgot.

1854
02:00:05,146 --> 02:00:11,105
<i>It's no good having you</i>

1855
02:00:11,563 --> 02:00:17,230
<i>If I don't have your whole heart</i>

1856
02:00:18,230 --> 02:00:24,812
<i>For this is love, you know</i>

1857
02:00:24,813 --> 02:00:30,438
<i>Not a prison sentence</i>

1858
02:00:31,271 --> 02:00:34,230
<i>Can putting it into words</i>

1859
02:00:34,646 --> 02:00:37,646
<i>Show you the pain in my heart?</i>

1860
02:00:37,938 --> 02:00:44,063
<i>Will I ever find a way
To tell it all to you?</i>

1861
02:00:44,480 --> 02:00:50,605
<i>Even if I'm never truly yours</i>

1862
02:00:51,105 --> 02:00:57,188
<i>Will you remember me by chance?</i>

1863
02:00:57,688 --> 02:01:03,563
<i>You…</i>

1864
02:01:04,480 --> 02:01:07,979
<i>I loved you while I lived and breathed</i>

1865
02:01:07,980 --> 02:01:13,605
<i>I'll love you after death</i>

1866
02:01:17,646 --> 02:01:24,355
<i>Even if fate keeps us apart
I'll love you my every breath</i>

1867
02:01:27,396 --> 02:01:34,105
<i>You can leave me</i>

1868
02:01:34,605 --> 02:01:38,688
<i>For somebody new</i>

1869
02:01:40,605 --> 02:01:47,271
<i>I'll accept it all</i>

1870
02:01:47,855 --> 02:01:52,480
<i>For the sake of you</i>

1871
02:01:53,521 --> 02:01:59,938
<i>Even through my tears
I'll try to make you smile</i>

1872
02:02:00,480 --> 02:02:07,146
<i>If I've chosen love
Then I must stand by it all the while</i>

1873
02:02:13,271 --> 02:02:19,355
<i>You are my whole life too</i>

1874
02:02:19,813 --> 02:02:25,938
<i>Every prayer came true for me</i>

1875
02:02:26,480 --> 02:02:32,563
<i>The day I found you</i>

1876
02:02:33,021 --> 02:02:39,105
<i>You…</i>

1877
02:02:39,855 --> 02:02:43,146
<i>I loved you while I lived and breathed</i>

1878
02:02:43,313 --> 02:02:49,688
<i>I'll love you after death</i>

1879
02:02:53,146 --> 02:02:59,688
<i>Even if fate keeps us apart
I'll love you my every breath</i>

1880
02:03:42,646 --> 02:03:43,938
Diya, you called me?

1881
02:03:46,063 --> 02:03:46,938
Wanted to give you this.

1882
02:03:49,063 --> 02:03:49,938
Why?

1883
02:03:50,521 --> 02:03:52,480
The wedding chain should stay
with the groom.

1884
02:03:52,896 --> 02:03:54,396
Otherwise, what'll he put around
the bride's neck?

1885
02:04:05,938 --> 02:04:07,396
It looked nice on her, right?

1886
02:04:11,230 --> 02:04:12,480
She'll have to wear it her whole life.

1887
02:04:14,063 --> 02:04:15,063
What are you saying?

1888
02:04:16,230 --> 02:04:17,521
Let's not do this, baby.

1889
02:04:20,021 --> 02:04:20,896
It's okay.

1890
02:04:21,896 --> 02:04:22,855
It really is.

1891
02:04:24,521 --> 02:04:25,521
You fell in love.

1892
02:04:26,813 --> 02:04:29,063
It really doesn't make you a bad person.

1893
02:04:31,355 --> 02:04:32,605
You didn't plan it.

1894
02:04:33,938 --> 02:04:35,271
In fact, this is my fault.

1895
02:04:35,896 --> 02:04:37,146
If I hadn't taken you to Sicily,

1896
02:04:37,688 --> 02:04:38,896
you would've never met Ally.

1897
02:04:39,855 --> 02:04:41,980
- Diya, it's not like that.
- Baby…

1898
02:04:42,771 --> 02:04:44,188
I know you well.

1899
02:04:45,688 --> 02:04:49,813
You avoid hurting people,
no matter what it costs you.

1900
02:04:50,230 --> 02:04:51,563
That's why I love you.

1901
02:04:53,438 --> 02:04:58,188
But don't marry me
out of a sense of responsibility

1902
02:04:59,063 --> 02:05:00,438
if your heart isn't in it.

1903
02:05:03,188 --> 02:05:04,230
Actually, you know what?

1904
02:05:06,771 --> 02:05:09,605
I've never seen you this unhappy.

1905
02:05:11,855 --> 02:05:13,855
I don't want to be the reason for that.

1906
02:05:15,730 --> 02:05:18,146
I only want to be the reason
for your happiness.

1907
02:05:19,313 --> 02:05:21,854
And if someone else gives
you that happiness,

1908
02:05:21,855 --> 02:05:23,146
how can I stop you?

1909
02:05:24,771 --> 02:05:26,396
And just because I love you,

1910
02:05:27,146 --> 02:05:30,479
and you can't tell me
you don't feel the same,

1911
02:05:30,480 --> 02:05:33,771
I can't pretend I don't know the truth.

1912
02:05:38,230 --> 02:05:39,146
Okay.

1913
02:05:47,813 --> 02:05:51,396
It feels like everyone here
already knows how I feel.

1914
02:05:52,730 --> 02:05:54,146
You've already decided

1915
02:05:55,646 --> 02:05:57,480
who I love and who I don't.

1916
02:06:06,188 --> 02:06:07,313
So you tell me.

1917
02:06:09,438 --> 02:06:10,438
Do you love her?

1918
02:06:34,271 --> 02:06:35,938
You know I love you.

1919
02:06:36,438 --> 02:06:38,770
I can see you love me.

1920
02:06:38,771 --> 02:06:40,645
- If you don't, then just say so.
- Ma'am!

1921
02:06:40,646 --> 02:06:41,937
- Like, why are you so scared?
- Excuse me, ma'am!

1922
02:06:41,938 --> 02:06:42,895
What?!

1923
02:06:42,896 --> 02:06:44,355
There's someone here to see you
at the reception.

1924
02:06:47,938 --> 02:06:48,980
Mom? Dad?

1925
02:06:49,313 --> 02:06:50,270
Hi, dear!

1926
02:06:50,271 --> 02:06:51,230
- Alisha!
- Hi!

1927
02:06:54,271 --> 02:06:55,687
What are you doing here?

1928
02:06:55,688 --> 02:06:57,521
Your friend Diya called us.

1929
02:06:57,938 --> 02:07:00,687
She said there was a big surprise.

1930
02:07:00,688 --> 02:07:02,396
And told us not to tell you.

1931
02:07:02,980 --> 02:07:05,521
So, what's the surprise?

1932
02:07:05,813 --> 02:07:06,688
Tell us.

1933
02:07:08,355 --> 02:07:09,521
I'll just be back.

1934
02:07:10,230 --> 02:07:11,105
- Alisha?
- Alisha?

1935
02:07:11,230 --> 02:07:12,271
That bitch!

1936
02:07:14,396 --> 02:07:15,355
What's happening?

1937
02:07:20,646 --> 02:07:21,979
Diya, what is going on?

1938
02:07:21,980 --> 02:07:23,730
Why did you call my parents?

1939
02:07:23,896 --> 02:07:25,355
- Listen--
- One second, Diya, please.

1940
02:07:27,355 --> 02:07:28,729
Let's just take this outside.

1941
02:07:28,730 --> 02:07:29,730
Wait, son.

1942
02:07:29,938 --> 02:07:31,813
- Diya!
- At least tell us what's going on.

1943
02:07:31,938 --> 02:07:35,104
- You say something!
- How can they do this to us now?

1944
02:07:35,105 --> 02:07:36,105
- How…
- Yeah…

1945
02:07:41,771 --> 02:07:43,146
She thinks…

1946
02:07:45,730 --> 02:07:46,896
I love you…

1947
02:07:48,980 --> 02:07:53,188
and I'm marrying her only
out of a sense of responsibility.

1948
02:07:54,480 --> 02:07:55,396
Am I wrong?

1949
02:08:02,480 --> 02:08:03,355
You're not.

1950
02:08:05,146 --> 02:08:06,188
But he'll never say it.

1951
02:08:06,938 --> 02:08:08,438
What if someone feels bad?

1952
02:08:08,688 --> 02:08:09,979
Someone's feelings get hurt?

1953
02:08:09,980 --> 02:08:12,313
- Someone's image gets ruined?
- I'm not talking to you.

1954
02:08:14,271 --> 02:08:15,605
Today he'll have to answer.

1955
02:08:15,813 --> 02:08:16,938
What do you want to hear?

1956
02:08:18,146 --> 02:08:20,021
You only wanna hear
what you wanna hear.

1957
02:08:36,980 --> 02:08:38,480
You still won't answer me?

1958
02:08:43,688 --> 02:08:45,396
Whose feelings are you protecting now?

1959
02:08:46,771 --> 02:08:50,021
At least respect me enough
to tell me the truth to my face.

1960
02:08:51,438 --> 02:08:54,105
Just tell me the truth,

1961
02:08:54,605 --> 02:08:56,105
and I'll leave happily.

1962
02:08:56,230 --> 02:08:57,271
Oh, please!

1963
02:08:57,396 --> 02:09:00,188
Stop acting like the victim.

1964
02:09:00,355 --> 02:09:01,980
And don't even talk about respect.

1965
02:09:02,230 --> 02:09:03,687
You respect him, right?

1966
02:09:03,688 --> 02:09:05,563
That's why you asked me to seduce him?

1967
02:09:06,730 --> 02:09:09,104
To test his loyalty?

1968
02:09:09,105 --> 02:09:10,646
Why didn't you ask him directly then?

1969
02:09:13,771 --> 02:09:16,480
Out of decency, I said nothing happened.

1970
02:09:17,021 --> 02:09:18,813
But it's not like nothing happened.

1971
02:09:19,230 --> 02:09:20,230
Tell him.

1972
02:09:20,521 --> 02:09:21,521
What is she talking about?

1973
02:09:22,105 --> 02:09:23,854
- Kunal…
- Tell him. Tell him the truth.

1974
02:09:23,855 --> 02:09:24,896
Is she telling the truth?

1975
02:09:28,771 --> 02:09:29,730
Kunal, baby…

1976
02:09:30,188 --> 02:09:32,396
Baby, I fucked up.

1977
02:09:32,896 --> 02:09:33,771
I'm sorry.

1978
02:09:34,146 --> 02:09:35,812
I just wanted to know

1979
02:09:35,813 --> 02:09:38,355
if you really wanted to be with me.

1980
02:09:40,605 --> 02:09:41,480
I'm sorry.

1981
02:09:42,438 --> 02:09:43,730
What happened was wrong.

1982
02:09:44,105 --> 02:09:46,604
I have no excuses.

1983
02:09:46,605 --> 02:09:48,645
But my intentions weren't bad.

1984
02:09:48,646 --> 02:09:50,855
- And you just played along?
- Only in the beginning.

1985
02:09:51,438 --> 02:09:53,813
Kunal, then-- Then I really
started feeling for you.

1986
02:09:53,980 --> 02:09:55,188
Everything was real.

1987
02:09:55,396 --> 02:09:57,229
- Every single bit of it, I swear.
- Kunal…

1988
02:09:57,230 --> 02:09:58,480
Kunal, just listen to me.

1989
02:09:58,813 --> 02:10:00,521
- Kunal, just listen to me!
- Don't even try!

1990
02:10:03,396 --> 02:10:04,271
Please.

1991
02:10:07,021 --> 02:10:12,146
<i>Every flaw in you</i>

1992
02:10:13,396 --> 02:10:19,188
<i>I'd still forgive</i>

1993
02:10:19,855 --> 02:10:25,313
<i>Even if it's wrong</i>

1994
02:10:26,313 --> 02:10:29,813
<i>- I'd relive it…</i>
- I won't say a word.

1995
02:10:30,271 --> 02:10:31,355
I'll keep quiet.

1996
02:10:32,230 --> 02:10:34,146
I can't leave you alone.

1997
02:10:35,896 --> 02:10:42,104
{\an8}<i>What can I do?
My love's gone wild</i>

1998
02:10:42,105 --> 02:10:48,730
<i>This is how my heart speaks its mind</i>

1999
02:10:48,980 --> 02:10:50,271
What did you gain from all this?

2000
02:10:51,730 --> 02:10:55,979
I called your parents here thinking
that if he admitted his feelings,

2001
02:10:55,980 --> 02:10:57,355
you two could finally be together!

2002
02:10:59,396 --> 02:11:02,354
I can really accept that
Kunal doesn't love me.

2003
02:11:02,355 --> 02:11:05,229
But if he also loses respect for me,

2004
02:11:05,230 --> 02:11:08,479
I swear to God, I will not forgive myself,
and I will not forgive you!

2005
02:11:08,480 --> 02:11:10,437
You could've told me
what you were doing!

2006
02:11:10,438 --> 02:11:11,770
Seeing Mom and Dad here suddenly,

2007
02:11:11,771 --> 02:11:14,479
I couldn't figure out your plan.
I panicked, man!

2008
02:11:14,480 --> 02:11:17,104
- You're such an idiot!
- I know! I know! I know!

2009
02:11:17,105 --> 02:11:19,145
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
I know it was our secret.

2010
02:11:19,146 --> 02:11:21,187
I shouldn't have told Kunal.

2011
02:11:21,188 --> 02:11:23,270
And now I know your
intentions weren't wrong.

2012
02:11:23,271 --> 02:11:24,688
Go tell him that!

2013
02:11:24,938 --> 02:11:27,354
He's not going to do
something stupid, right?

2014
02:11:27,355 --> 02:11:29,437
Why would he kill himself
over our stupidity?

2015
02:11:29,438 --> 02:11:30,395
Kill himself?!

2016
02:11:30,396 --> 02:11:32,437
What is wrong with you?
You jumped straight to suicide?!

2017
02:11:32,438 --> 02:11:34,020
Then what did you mean
by "do something stupid"?

2018
02:11:34,021 --> 02:11:36,062
I don't know! Stop yelling!
I'm freaking out!

2019
02:11:36,063 --> 02:11:37,229
You think I'm not freaking out?!

2020
02:11:37,230 --> 02:11:38,770
Ma'am, I'm here for the bride's makeup.

2021
02:11:38,771 --> 02:11:39,688
- Shut up!
- Shut up!

2022
02:11:49,855 --> 02:11:50,730
Where are you going?

2023
02:11:51,188 --> 02:11:52,313
To find him. Where else?

2024
02:11:52,771 --> 02:11:54,355
Why are you going? I'll go.

2025
02:11:54,605 --> 02:11:55,562
Why?

2026
02:11:55,563 --> 02:11:58,438
You already said you'd leave
if he admitted his feelings.

2027
02:11:58,855 --> 02:12:00,521
Well, did he admit it?
No, right?

2028
02:12:00,646 --> 02:12:02,479
- He didn't!
- You already know how he feels.

2029
02:12:02,480 --> 02:12:04,021
That's why you called my parents.

2030
02:12:04,396 --> 02:12:05,313
How noble of you!

2031
02:12:17,271 --> 02:12:20,105
I'm with him. Can't talk right now.

2032
02:12:23,230 --> 02:12:24,188
Oh, boy!

2033
02:12:28,980 --> 02:12:31,062
I'm with him. Can't talk.

2034
02:12:31,063 --> 02:12:32,521
We agreed you wouldn't say a word.

2035
02:12:33,355 --> 02:12:34,812
I'm not talking to you.

2036
02:12:34,813 --> 02:12:36,062
Hang up! Keep it down!

2037
02:12:36,063 --> 02:12:37,063
Fine.

2038
02:12:45,230 --> 02:12:46,105
Oh!

2039
02:12:47,813 --> 02:12:48,813
Give me the keys!

2040
02:12:49,480 --> 02:12:50,355
Whose car is it?

2041
02:12:54,688 --> 02:12:55,563
Open the door.

2042
02:12:56,563 --> 02:12:57,438
It's open.

2043
02:12:57,688 --> 02:12:58,729
Open the door.

2044
02:12:58,730 --> 02:13:00,021
Open!

2045
02:13:00,438 --> 02:13:01,313
Okay.

2046
02:13:01,730 --> 02:13:02,646
Fine.

2047
02:13:05,105 --> 02:13:06,063
You…

2048
02:13:06,855 --> 02:13:08,230
Diya!
Diya!

2049
02:13:13,438 --> 02:13:14,563
"Have a couple of drinks
and sleep it off."

2050
02:13:15,063 --> 02:13:16,855
"We'll play <i>antakshari</i> on the bus."

2051
02:13:17,438 --> 02:13:19,521
"Then all the rituals will happen.
It'll all be over before you know it."

2052
02:13:21,730 --> 02:13:22,896
Amazing father you are.

2053
02:13:23,563 --> 02:13:25,563
Why are you angry at me?
What did I do…

2054
02:13:26,563 --> 02:13:29,021
besides giving you good genes?

2055
02:13:30,063 --> 02:13:31,896
Two girls are fighting over you.

2056
02:13:50,813 --> 02:13:53,063
You know my intention
was never to hurt you.

2057
02:13:54,521 --> 02:13:55,438
I know.

2058
02:13:57,521 --> 02:13:58,854
He's just so lovable

2059
02:13:58,855 --> 02:14:01,396
that sacrificing a friendship
for him felt worth it.

2060
02:14:02,271 --> 02:14:05,605
Yeah, but you wouldn't do that
if you were me.

2061
02:14:11,396 --> 02:14:14,688
I'll never apologize for falling
in love with him.

2062
02:14:14,980 --> 02:14:16,813
- But for hurting you, I'm really--
- Drop it.

2063
02:14:19,730 --> 02:14:20,896
Doesn't suit you.

2064
02:14:29,230 --> 02:14:31,021
Whatever you decide,

2065
02:14:32,021 --> 02:14:33,146
hearts will be broken, son.

2066
02:14:35,730 --> 02:14:38,145
If you choose Diya,
Ally's heart will break.

2067
02:14:38,146 --> 02:14:40,813
If you choose Ally,
Diya's heart will break.

2068
02:14:42,063 --> 02:14:43,271
The family's hearts will break too.

2069
02:14:44,855 --> 02:14:46,105
Just don't break your own heart.

2070
02:14:47,855 --> 02:14:51,355
A man with a broken heart
can't keep anyone happy.

2071
02:14:53,938 --> 02:14:58,105
A broken heart makes life feel

2072
02:14:59,813 --> 02:15:00,980
unbearably heavy.

2073
02:15:12,730 --> 02:15:13,605
Get out.

2074
02:15:29,438 --> 02:15:30,313
Is that…

2075
02:15:30,688 --> 02:15:31,563
Yeah.

2076
02:15:32,813 --> 02:15:34,563
Where… where is he?

2077
02:15:35,105 --> 02:15:36,355
- Go, go, go!
- Yeah.

2078
02:15:48,521 --> 02:15:49,730
Kunal, stop the car!

2079
02:15:50,355 --> 02:15:51,230
Kunal!

2080
02:15:51,438 --> 02:15:52,313
Kunal!

2081
02:15:52,438 --> 02:15:53,687
Kunal, please stop the car!

2082
02:15:53,688 --> 02:15:54,895
Please stop the car!

2083
02:15:54,896 --> 02:15:55,771
- Kunal!
- Kunal!

2084
02:16:11,146 --> 02:16:13,896
<i>Eeny, meeny, miny, moe
Catch a tiger by the toe!</i>

2085
02:16:14,521 --> 02:16:15,396
Yeah?

2086
02:16:16,521 --> 02:16:18,105
No? Should we toss?

2087
02:16:19,563 --> 02:16:20,480
Got a coin?

2088
02:16:20,771 --> 02:16:21,938
Heads is her, tails is you.

2089
02:16:24,355 --> 02:16:25,438
Just answer me one thing, Diya.

2090
02:16:26,688 --> 02:16:27,771
Why'd you do it?

2091
02:16:28,855 --> 02:16:30,063
Just because of a joke?

2092
02:16:31,271 --> 02:16:32,937
You know why I could joke about it?

2093
02:16:32,938 --> 02:16:36,813
Because I never thought
you'd ever believe I'd cheat on you.

2094
02:16:39,605 --> 02:16:41,938
You broke my faith in us.

2095
02:16:42,271 --> 02:16:43,396
How did she ask you?

2096
02:16:45,271 --> 02:16:46,313
Jokingly?

2097
02:16:46,896 --> 02:16:47,855
To seduce me?

2098
02:16:48,771 --> 02:16:50,063
And you just laughed and agreed?

2099
02:16:53,063 --> 02:16:55,605
You both made me into a joke.

2100
02:17:04,230 --> 02:17:05,105
Sorry…

2101
02:17:14,188 --> 02:17:15,146
This is what happens

2102
02:17:15,521 --> 02:17:17,771
when people consume
too much social media nonsense.

2103
02:17:19,021 --> 02:17:21,146
"Couples should know everything
about each other."

2104
02:17:21,396 --> 02:17:23,355
"Give us five reasons
why you like each other."

2105
02:17:24,313 --> 02:17:26,688
"A relationship should
always remain exciting."

2106
02:17:27,771 --> 02:17:29,771
If excitement is what defines love,

2107
02:17:30,105 --> 02:17:31,855
then maybe love isn't that deep after all.

2108
02:17:34,771 --> 02:17:38,813
Every relationship feels exciting at first
because it's new.

2109
02:17:40,938 --> 02:17:44,104
New friends are fun too because
their stories are new to you.

2110
02:17:44,105 --> 02:17:46,230
Old friends' stories bore you
after a while.

2111
02:17:49,230 --> 02:17:51,188
You can be in love with anything
for a few days.

2112
02:17:53,896 --> 02:17:54,896
But, Diya…

2113
02:17:56,813 --> 02:17:58,480
love is like that worn-out T-shirt

2114
02:18:00,688 --> 02:18:02,688
you sleep best in.

2115
02:18:10,188 --> 02:18:11,105
And yes…

2116
02:18:12,313 --> 02:18:13,521
I do feel love for her.

2117
02:18:13,813 --> 02:18:14,730
She's lovely.

2118
02:18:17,771 --> 02:18:21,646
And maybe, in another life,
if we'd met sooner…

2119
02:18:24,563 --> 02:18:25,813
we could've been together.

2120
02:18:31,021 --> 02:18:32,021
But "maybe"

2121
02:18:33,521 --> 02:18:35,188
is a huge thing.

2122
02:18:37,688 --> 02:18:38,895
Maybe after six months,

2123
02:18:38,896 --> 02:18:40,355
we wouldn't even be able
to tolerate each other.

2124
02:18:43,938 --> 02:18:45,980
There's no "maybe" between her and me.

2125
02:18:47,021 --> 02:18:48,730
That's exactly why you and I are us, Diya.

2126
02:18:52,188 --> 02:18:53,063
You're like

2127
02:18:54,146 --> 02:18:56,646
my overflowing cupboard.

2128
02:18:56,771 --> 02:18:59,438
Mom sees it and says, "What a mess!"

2129
02:18:59,563 --> 02:19:01,855
But I can reach in blind

2130
02:19:04,271 --> 02:19:05,730
and find exactly what I need.

2131
02:19:07,521 --> 02:19:08,396
You know why?

2132
02:19:11,355 --> 02:19:12,646
Because it's my cupboard.

2133
02:19:15,271 --> 02:19:16,438
Yes, your kind of wedding…

2134
02:19:17,396 --> 02:19:18,813
is more my type.

2135
02:19:20,105 --> 02:19:22,355
And I'm doing this one for her.
Do you know why?

2136
02:19:22,480 --> 02:19:25,480
Because the wedding lasts four days, Ally.

2137
02:19:29,021 --> 02:19:30,980
But the relationship lasts a lifetime.

2138
02:19:34,355 --> 02:19:35,230
It's true

2139
02:19:36,396 --> 02:19:40,855
we don't know every tiny thing
about each other anymore, Diya.

2140
02:19:42,813 --> 02:19:44,021
But the big things?

2141
02:19:47,771 --> 02:19:49,146
We know them all.

2142
02:19:55,396 --> 02:19:56,355
Maybe today…

2143
02:19:58,021 --> 02:19:59,480
you like my smile more than she does.

2144
02:20:01,563 --> 02:20:02,438
But, Ally…

2145
02:20:04,813 --> 02:20:05,771
for years now…

2146
02:20:08,438 --> 02:20:10,355
she sees my tears

2147
02:20:11,563 --> 02:20:12,771
before they even reach my eyes.

2148
02:20:18,896 --> 02:20:22,938
You're that worn-out T-shirt
my sleep's gotten addicted to, Diya.

2149
02:20:26,188 --> 02:20:28,438
People unfairly judge habits.

2150
02:20:28,855 --> 02:20:29,813
Habits are a good thing.

2151
02:20:31,688 --> 02:20:33,438
They are built on trust.

2152
02:20:38,813 --> 02:20:40,396
You can become the sparkle in my eyes.

2153
02:20:43,855 --> 02:20:44,855
But she…

2154
02:20:46,938 --> 02:20:47,980
is my peace.

2155
02:20:57,813 --> 02:21:00,438
Yeah, she's a little crazy for testing me.

2156
02:21:01,730 --> 02:21:02,980
But you know what?

2157
02:21:03,688 --> 02:21:05,355
After all the madness
of mine you've tolerated…

2158
02:21:07,688 --> 02:21:08,563
you've earned the right.

2159
02:21:11,563 --> 02:21:14,980
You're not doing this just out of
a sense of responsibility, right?

2160
02:21:16,105 --> 02:21:16,980
I am.

2161
02:21:18,938 --> 02:21:21,021
It's responsibility, not a burden.

2162
02:21:21,646 --> 02:21:23,855
I want to be responsible for you, Diya.

2163
02:21:24,021 --> 02:21:25,063
That's why I'm doing this.

2164
02:21:26,605 --> 02:21:27,855
But there's one thing I'll never do.

2165
02:21:30,313 --> 02:21:32,730
I'll never tell you
what happened that night.

2166
02:21:35,813 --> 02:21:36,855
If you're still

2167
02:21:38,855 --> 02:21:40,355
willing to tolerate me,

2168
02:21:42,563 --> 02:21:43,938
then I'm around for this lifetime…

2169
02:21:46,688 --> 02:21:48,521
and all the lifetimes to come.

2170
02:21:58,230 --> 02:22:04,188
<i>You're the reason I still breathe</i>

2171
02:22:04,605 --> 02:22:09,688
<i>I live my life for you</i>

2172
02:22:10,896 --> 02:22:16,980
<i>How do I put in words</i>

2173
02:22:17,146 --> 02:22:22,230
<i>What I feel for you?</i>

2174
02:22:23,563 --> 02:22:29,521
<i>Nowhere in this world will anyone</i>

2175
02:22:29,855 --> 02:22:35,855
<i>- Ever love you…
- Quite this way</i>

2176
02:22:36,146 --> 02:22:42,021
<i>- No one else will…
- Give their heart</i>

2177
02:22:42,521 --> 02:22:47,396
<i>- Completely…
- Each passing day</i>

2178
02:22:55,021 --> 02:22:56,188
In this lifetime, he's yours.

2179
02:22:57,896 --> 02:22:59,105
In every lifetime, he's mine.

2180
02:23:01,646 --> 02:23:02,605
We'll see.

2181
02:23:29,313 --> 02:23:30,396
What are you guys waiting for?

2182
02:23:31,105 --> 02:23:32,396
We have a wedding to celebrate!

2183
02:23:37,355 --> 02:23:41,230
<i>These matters of fate</i>

2184
02:23:43,771 --> 02:23:47,771
<i>Only fate can explain</i>

2185
02:23:50,063 --> 02:23:55,230
<i>For me, without you</i>

2186
02:23:56,521 --> 02:24:01,271
<i>Nothing else remains</i>

2187
02:24:02,980 --> 02:24:08,146
<i>My eyes may fill with tears</i>

2188
02:24:09,438 --> 02:24:13,521
<i>But I'll hide all the pain</i>

2189
02:24:15,730 --> 02:24:18,896
<i>If you're happy</i>

2190
02:24:19,146 --> 02:24:21,521
<i>Then for your happiness</i>

2191
02:24:22,105 --> 02:24:27,063
<i>I'll celebrate the same</i>

2192
02:24:28,521 --> 02:24:33,896
<i>But I'll keep loving you</i>

2193
02:24:34,980 --> 02:24:40,146
<i>Forever and more</i>

2194
02:24:41,355 --> 02:24:46,688
<i>I'll die loving you</i>

2195
02:24:47,688 --> 02:24:53,480
<i>Forever and more</i>

2196
02:24:54,188 --> 02:24:56,813
<i>Forever and more</i>

2197
02:24:57,313 --> 02:25:00,188
<i>Forever and more</i>

2198
02:25:00,563 --> 02:25:05,771
<i>Forever and more</i>

2199
02:25:08,355 --> 02:25:11,896
<i>My friend…</i>

2200
02:25:15,730 --> 02:25:16,688
I can't.

2201
02:25:25,438 --> 02:25:26,438
I can't.

2202
02:25:44,105 --> 02:25:47,354
<i>Forever and more</i>

2203
02:25:47,355 --> 02:25:50,771
<i>My heartstrings are tied to you</i>

2204
02:26:07,855 --> 02:26:11,105
You know, I'd have no problem
marrying a divorced man.

2205
02:26:11,646 --> 02:26:14,355
So if things don't work out,
don't worry about it.

2206
02:26:14,521 --> 02:26:15,438
You've got me.

2207
02:26:15,980 --> 02:26:17,646
Babe, are you done?

2208
02:26:19,480 --> 02:26:20,396
Yeah.

2209
02:26:25,021 --> 02:26:26,062
Come on, fast.

2210
02:26:26,063 --> 02:26:27,105
Come fast, come.

